.TH ZERODDS-ZENOH-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-zenoh-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-zenoh-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/zenoh-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the Zenoh bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto
Zenoh key expressions. Read by the shared layered loader
.RI ( zerodds-config ):
this file, a sibling
.IR zenoh-bridged.d/ ,
.BR include: ,
.BI ${VAR}
substitution, with the precedence defaults < environment < files <
.BR \-\-set .
An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the wrong shape or
type, stops the start with the file and line.
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " zenoh ", " discovery ", " limits ", " metrics ", "
.BR topics .
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
A
.B \-\-log\-level
on the command line wins over this key.
.SS zenoh
.TP
.B mode
.IR peer " (default) | " client " | " router .
.TP
.BR connect ", " listen
Lists of Zenoh endpoint strings, e.g.
.IR "tcp/192.0.2.10:7447" .
.TP
.B scouting.multicast.enabled
Boolean, default
.IR true .
.B false
matches
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
\&'s
.BR \-\-no\-multicast\-scouting .
.TP
.B scope
The Zenoh key-expression scope (a string, default empty). Every routed key
expression is
.IR <scope>/<partition>/<topic> ,
with
.B scope
and the topic's
.B partition
each optional \(em the default (empty scope) matches
.BR zenoh-plugin-dds 's
own default exactly, so a bridge on one site and a
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
on another interoperate without extra configuration. Set to
.I "dds"
to reproduce the historic ZeroDDS-only layout instead.
.TP
.B reliable_routes_blocking
Boolean, default
.IR true .
Whether a Zenoh
.B put
re-publishing a sample from a
.B RELIABLE
DDS writer uses
.B CongestionControl::Block
(backpressure) instead of
.B ::Drop
\(em matches
.BR zenoh-plugin-dds 's
own default.
.TP
.B queries_timeout_ms
Integer, default
.IR 5000 .
Timeout for the query a
.B TRANSIENT_LOCAL
Zenoh\(->DDS route issues at declaration time to fetch retained samples from
existing
.B PublicationCache
queryables (the late-joiner path). Matches the plugin's
.B queries_timeout
default of 5.0 s.
.TP
.B config_file
Optional path to a full Zenoh JSON5/YAML5 config file (TLS, auth, transport
tuning) loaded as the base
.BR zenoh::Config ;
.BR mode / connect / listen / scouting
above are applied over it, the same layering
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
itself uses.
.SS discovery
.TP
.B auto_bridge
Boolean, default
.IR true .
Bridges every DDS topic the daemon discovers via the DCPS built-in topics,
the way
.B zenoh-plugin-dds
bridges every topic it sees. Reloadable via SIGHUP.
.TP
.B poll_interval_ms
Integer, default
.IR 1000 .
The longest time between two passes of the discovery loop. A pass also
runs whenever the DDS runtime discovers or loses a publication or
subscription, or receives a peer's type (TypeLookup reply); a newly
discovered topic is bridged without waiting for this interval.
.TP
.BR allow ", " deny
Lists of
.IR * / ? " glob patterns (not regular expressions \(em this project's other"
allow/deny lists use the same convention) matched against the
.I derived
key expression. An empty
.B allow
means everything is allowed (matching the plugin's own
.B allow: None
default);
.B deny
wins over
.BR allow .
Reloadable via SIGHUP.
.PP
A topic discovered only as a publication (or only as a subscription) is
bridged one-way; the opposite side appearing later does not retroactively
widen it to
.B bidir
\(em list the topic explicitly under
.B topics:
with
.B direction: bidir
to guarantee both directions from the start. An auto-discovered topic
carries no type information, so it is always bridged as
.BR keyed: false .
.SS limits
.TP
.B max_payload_bytes
Integer, default
.IR 1048576 " (1 MiB)."
A DDS sample larger than this is refused \(em logged and counted, never
silently truncated.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9097"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one host
without a collision.
.SS topics (list)
A bare string entry is shorthand for
.BR "{dds_name: <string>}" .
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
DDS IDL type name. Default: same as
.BR dds_name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " (Zenoh\(->DDS) | " out " (DDS\(->Zenoh) | " bidir .
Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B partition
DDS partition; adds a key-expression segment
.RI ( <scope>/<partition>/<topic> ).
Default: none.
.TP
.B key_expr
Overrides the derived key expression with an explicit one.
.TP
.B keyed
Boolean, default
.IR false .
Whether the topic has one or more
.B @key
fields.
.TP
.B type_file
Path to a
.B CompleteTypeObject
blob (e.g. produced by
.BR zerodds-idlc ),
read at registration time. Required when
.B keyed
is true and
.B direction
is
.I in
or
.IR bidir :
without it, an incoming Zenoh sample's DDS key hash cannot be derived, and
.B write_user_sample_keyed
would collapse every instance onto the one default key \(em the daemon
refuses to load such a topic instead of doing that silently.
.SS topics[].qos
.TP
.B reliability
.IR reliable " (default) | " best_effort .
.TP
.B durability
.IR volatile " (default) | " transient_local " | " transient " | " persistent .
.B transient_local
turns on the late-joiner path (a
.B PublicationCache
DDS\(->Zenoh, a
.B FetchingSubscriber
Zenoh\(->DDS) \(em matches
.BR zenoh-plugin-dds ,
which checks only
.B TRANSIENT_LOCAL
(not
.BR transient / persistent ).
.TP
.B extensibility
.IR final " (default) | " appendable " | " mutable .
The topic root type's extensibility (XTypes 1.3 \(sc7.2.2), which picks the
RTPS encapsulation header on the Zenoh side (plain CDR/CDR2, delimited
D_CDR2, or parameter-list PL_CDR/PL_CDR2 \(em DDSI-RTPS 2.5 \(sc10.5 Table
10.3). A byte-forwarding daemon cannot discover this from the wire alone;
get it wrong and a real DDS peer on the far end of a chained
.B zenoh-bridge-dds
would misparse the body.
.TP
.B history.depth
Integer >= 1, default
.IR 1 .
.B PublicationCache
/
.B FetchingSubscriber
history depth for a
.B transient_local
topic (matches
.BR zenoh_ext 's
own
.B PublicationCacheBuilder
default).
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/zenoh-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-zenoh-bridged (1).
